   338                        ; *******S 
   339                        ;ASM version of subroutine to process IRQ when ACIA receives data 
   340                        ; replaced by C function " interrupt void IRQHandler(void); " in C_TEMPLATE_816.c
   341                        ; Every time a character is received by the ACIA, an IRQ interrupt is generated and 
   342                        ; this IRQ handler routine is run, putting the ASCII code of the char in the circular buffer. 
   343                        ; The WR_PTR is used as the destination index into the circular buffer, incremented each 
   344                        ; time a new interrupt is generated and wrapping around after 256 chars received. 
   345                        ; The C main function reads the characters from the buffer and processes them. 
   346                        ; !!! If not processed on time, the WR_PTR could wrap around and overwrite unprocessed chars.
  Mon Nov  2 2026  0:10                                                                                                    Page 8


   347                        ; Modifies: CPU flags, A, X, Y 
   348                        ; N_IRQ: 
   349                        		; REP #$30 			; 16 bit register A/X/Y so we save A/B and MSB/LSB of X/Y 
   350                        		; LONGA ON 			; and tell assembler about it 
   351                        		; LONGI ON 			; 
   352                        		; PHA					; save A/B, X and Y registers 
   353                        		; PHX					; since interrupt handler 
   354                        
   355                        							; If there are multiple IRQ sources, we need to chec
                    k which 
   356                        							; source generated the IRQ so we can handle it a ded
                    icated 
   357                        							; handler routine. We have only one source, so we ca
                    n skip. 
   358                        
   359                        		; LDA ACIA_DATA		; char in RX DATA REGISTER into A register 
   360                        		; LDX WR_IDX		; offset for destination in circular buffer 
   361                        		; STA $1000,X		; save char into circular buffer 
   362                        		; INC WR_IDX		; prep offset for next char 
   363                        
   364                        		; REP #$30 			; st A/X/Y back to 16 bit sizes 
   365                        		; LONGA ON 			; and tell assembler about it 
   366                        		; LONGI ON 			
   367                        		
   368                        		; PLX					; restore X and A/B registers 
   369                        		; PLA
   370                        
   371                        		; RTI 				; return from interrupt
   372                        ; *******E
